      "lineNbr": 463,
      "author": {
        "id": 1867527
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-03-12T03:53:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The two u64 parameters are used to tell kswapd how to age this lrugen, for example, whether the lrugen is skipped, what is the max_seq that was skipped last time, etc.\n\nThe other four u64s are used for two list heads to store some special pages, such as the file pages that have just been pre-read or the pages with high access frequency.",
